    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0460" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW(Peace)/1–2847</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Australia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Butler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 99</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canberra</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-28">January 28,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s telegram no. 279 of December 13, 1946, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d366-f1"/> wherein I was instructed to advise Dr. Evatt<anchor
                        n="62" xml:id="d366-f2"/> informally and confidentially that the United
                    States hoped and desired that Australia would participate on a full and equal
                    basis in the formulation of the peace treaty with Japan, and to my telegraphic
                    reply, no. 36 of January 28, 1947, 9 a.m.,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d366-f3"/>
                    summarizing the content of a letter addressed to me on January 17, 1947 by Dr.
                    Evatt, expressing appreciation of the message referred to above and outlining
                    his Government’s thoughts with respect to Japanese peace treaty negotiations. I
                    am forwarding herewith a copy of the text of Dr. Evatt’s letter.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert L. Butler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d366-a1.xml" xpointer="d366-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
